From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: move the VLAN list also when one link remains

Upstream fix: hostap main 741d70dd8e32 has the same code, from
aa7a038e088f ("AP MLD: Move VLAN list when the first link (BSS) is
removed"); to be reported upstream.

An AP MLD keeps its VLAN list on the first BSS, and every VLAN user
takes it from hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(). hostapd_mld_remove_link()
moved the list to the new first BSS only where that BSS is not the last
link. When the first of two links is removed, the remaining link became
the first BSS with its own list, which holds only the wildcard entry:

- a GTK rekey of a VLAN group fails in hostapd_wpa_auth_set_key(), as
  the list has no interface for the VLAN ID, and the group state
  machine ends in FATAL_FAILURE;
- vlan_remove_dynamic() finds no entry, so the AP_VLAN netdev stays
  after its last station, and the next station of that VLAN fails in
  vlan_add_dynamic() because the netdev exists.

Move the list for every new first BSS, and free the new first BSS's own
list, which the AP MLD no longer reads. This also stops the leak of that
list on the path with more links.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ap_config.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_config.c
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 #include "ap_config.h"
 
 
-static void hostapd_config_free_vlan(struct hostapd_bss_config *bss)
+void hostapd_config_free_vlan(struct hostapd_bss_config *bss)
 {
 	struct hostapd_vlan *vlan, *prev;
 
--- a/src/ap/ap_config.h
+++ b/src/ap/ap_config.h
@@ -1498,6 +1498,7 @@ void hostapd_config_free_eap_user(struct
 void hostapd_config_free_eap_users(struct hostapd_eap_user *user);
 void hostapd_config_clear_wpa_psk(struct hostapd_wpa_psk **p);
 void hostapd_config_clear_rxkhs(struct hostapd_bss_config *conf);
+void hostapd_config_free_vlan(struct hostapd_bss_config *bss);
 void hostapd_config_free_bss(struct hostapd_bss_config *conf);
 void hostapd_config_free(struct hostapd_config *conf);
 int hostapd_maclist_found(struct mac_acl_entry *list, int num_entries,
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1718,14 +1718,15 @@ void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hosta
 /* hostapd_mld_move_vlan_list - Move the VLAN list to the new first bss
  *
  * This function is used to copy the reference to the VLAN list from the old
- * first BSS to the new first BSS when the first BSS is removed.
+ * first BSS to the new first BSS when the first BSS is removed. The AP MLD
+ * uses only the list of its first BSS, so the new first BSS's own list goes.
  */
 static void hostapd_mld_move_vlan_list(struct hostapd_data *old_fbss,
 				       struct hostapd_data *new_fbss)
 {
+	hostapd_config_free_vlan(new_fbss->conf);
 	new_fbss->conf->vlan = old_fbss->conf->vlan;
 	old_fbss->conf->vlan = NULL;
-
 }
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
@@ -6814,16 +6815,9 @@ int hostapd_mld_remove_link(struct hosta
 	if (dl_list_empty(&mld->links)) {
 		mld->fbss = NULL;
 	} else {
-		struct hostapd_data *last_link_bss;
-
 		next_fbss = dl_list_entry(mld->links.next, struct hostapd_data,
 					  link);
-		last_link_bss = dl_list_last(&mld->links, struct hostapd_data,
-					     link);
-
-		if (next_fbss != last_link_bss)
-			hostapd_mld_move_vlan_list(hapd, next_fbss);
-
+		hostapd_mld_move_vlan_list(hapd, next_fbss);
 		mld->fbss = next_fbss;
 		hostapd_mld_move_radius(hapd, next_fbss);
 		accounting_mld_first_bss_moved(hapd, next_fbss);
